{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he struck your rear.</b> He pursued after those who were at the tail of the camp." "<b>The stragglers.</b> The weakened ones — from inverted letter forms, like כשבים / כבשים." "<b>And you were faint and weary.</b> Do not wonder if he did thus to you, for you were <b>faint and weary</b> from the exertion of the journey, and furthermore you were <b>not fearing Elohim</b>, as stated in the Mekhilta: others say, 'and did not fear Elohim' — these are Israel, in whom there were commandments and they did not fulfill them; but had you been fearers of Elohim, he could not have overcome you."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:16.026838597Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}